            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 1)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "5627dc6e-c943-439e-ab4a-4531b7f24264"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Origin of the Conflict</strong><br>\nThe Israel-Palestine conflict has deep roots that stretch far back into history. Various religious and ethnic groups have always coexisted in this region. The main actors in the conflict are often Jews, Muslims, and Christians. The religious differences are deeply ingrained and strongly influence the identities and views of the people in the region.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Significance of Jerusalem</strong><br>\nJerusalem is a central point of the conflict. For Jews, it is the home of the Temple Mount, the holiest site in Judaism. For Muslims, it is the place from which the Prophet Mohammed is believed to have ascended to heaven. And for Christians, it is the site of the crucifixion and resurrection of Jesus Christ. The religious significance of Jerusalem contributes to the intensity of the conflict.</p>\n\n<p><strong>State of Israel and Palestine</strong><br>\nThe establishment of the State of Israel in 1948 was a significant milestone that further inflamed the conflict. Many Palestinians were displaced or fled, and the territories were divided. Both sides, Israelis and Palestinians, claim the land for themselves and have deep religious and historical ties to it.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Religious Identity and Nationalism</strong><br>\nReligious identity is often closely linked with nationalism. For many people in the region, their religious affiliation is an important part of their national identity. This leads to a strong sense of belonging and protection of the land considered holy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Settlement Policy</strong><br>\nIsrael's settlement policy in the occupied territories is another flashpoint. Many settlers believe it is their religious duty to live in these areas, while many Palestinians view the land as their own. The settlements are often a trigger for tension and violence.</p>\n\n<p><strong>International Involvement</strong><br>\nThe international community has intervened in the conflict, often due to the religious significance of the region and its strategic location in the Middle East. Different countries have different interests and alliances, further complicating the dynamics of the conflict.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
